(Ord. No. 10-08, § 1, 4-27-10; Ord. No. 16-12, § 6, 12-13-16)

882:
The following fixtures, uses or application shall be exempt from the standards set forth in section 20-15-133:
(1) Showers and faucets installed for safety purposes, such as emergency eyewash stations, etc.;
(2) Plumbing fixtures specifically designed for use by the physically handicapped;
(3) Fixtures specifically designed to withstand unusual abuse or for installation in correctional institutions which may require more water for proper operation;
(4) Building renovations in which significant plumbing modifications would be required to accommodate the lower flows or for specialized purposes which cannot be accommodated by existing technology; permission for the exceptions listed in this subsection must be obtained from the building official of the city;
(5) One-piece toilets are exempt from the provisions of this article until July 1, 1992;
(6) Commercial buildings are exempt until July 1, 1992; and
(7) Juvenile toilet facilities.
(Ord. No. 91-14A, § 1(5), 6-11-91)
